      "content": "It is entirely understandable to feel depleted when the major motivator disappears; those deep-seated goals can sustain us for years. Instead of needing a giant, defining \"next goal,\" perhaps focus on very small, immediate shifts that bring a flicker of personal joy. Sometimes, finding worth in simple presence—a hobby, a quiet skill, or a single connection—can begin to fill that unexpected void.",
      "source": "target",
